        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Seacroft, Lincolnshire; Skegness; Gibraltar Point nature reserve; Lincolnshire, England\n- Features: Seacroft Esplanade; golf course; national nature reserve\n- Topics: geography\n\nFacts:\n- Seacroft, Lincolnshire lies south of and is joined to Skegness.\n- Seacroft, Lincolnshire comprises Seacroft Esplanade, a residential road less than half a mile long, and a golf course to its south.\n- Gibraltar Point nature reserve lies farther south of Seacroft, Lincolnshire.\n- Gibraltar Point national nature reserve is an area of approximately 4.3 square kilometres in Lincolnshire, England.",
